# The implicit-install gate for this project does NOT live here.
#
# pnpm's `verify-deps-before-run` defaults to `install`: running any script via
# `pnpm run` against a stale lockfile silently installs first, and installing
# reaches the network. On 2026-08-25 a `pnpm run check` did exactly that. This
# file then carried the gate as `verify-deps-before-run=warn` — and a measured
# probe on 2026-08-27 showed that value is INERT here: against REAL staleness
# (a dependency present in package.json that the lockfile lacks), `error` set
# in this file still spawned the install. The key's spelling does occur inside
# pnpm 11.17.0's bundle, so grepping the bundle proves nothing either way; the
# behavioural probe is the evidence.
#
# The live gate is `verifyDepsBeforeRun: warn` in pnpm-workspace.yaml, which
# the same probe showed IS honoured: `error` there refuses with
# ERR_PNPM_VERIFY_DEPS_BEFORE_RUN before the script runs, `warn` warns, runs,
# and installs nothing (lockfile byte-identical, store file count unchanged).
# Probe runs that could have installed were executed under
# `pnpm_config_offline=true`, so a wrong guess could not reach the network.
#
# LIMITS: the probe proves detection plus refuse/warn semantics against a
# manufactured missing-dependency staleness. The 2026-08-25 incident's
# staleness had a different cause (importer entries for packages already in
# the tree); interception of that exact path is not demonstrated.
#
# Full account: DESIGN.md §6. Transcript and 2-minute rerun recipe:
# evidence/npmrc-probe.txt (tracked; run records under goal-runs/ are
# machine-local and no longer ship, so cited evidence lives here)
#
# No settings live in this file. It exists so nobody re-adds the key here
# believing it works; dropping the old inert line also drops the
# `npm warn Unknown project config` noise every npx call printed.
